      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When it comes to equitable distribution of affordable housing units, an evidence-based approach could be the most effective. Research suggests that community-based selection methods, such as income-based priorities and lottery systems, have made significant impacts on refugee, homeless, and long-term low-income populations. However, a multi-pronged approach considering various factors, including proximity to transit, income, and community need, could provide a balanced solution. Some cities have also implemented a \"housing choice voucher\" system, allowing residents to choose from a set of available units based on priority needs and availability.",
