      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Practicing equality among the moderately needy would indeed be a compromise on the core purpose of an affordable housing mandate, which is to address the most pressing and dire housing crises. Prioritizing the unhoused and extremely low-income families acknowledges the severe hardships they face and recognizes that everyone deserves a basic standard of housing and dignity. By focusing on the most vulnerable first, you can demonstrate that the policy is committed to social justice and human rights, and that the needs of those most severely impacted are being addressed.",
